<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin introduces tobacco tax measures.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin introduces tobacco tax measures.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin introduced tobacco tax measures into the House of Commons on Thursday, a government official said.</p>
<p>No details were available but Martin was due to meet reporters at 1330 EST/1830 GMT.</p>
<p>Health Minister David Dingwall has been drawing up anti-tobacco measures which were expected to include tax increases. The taxation would require Martin's involvement.</p>
</text>
